            <ArticleTitle>Regulation of metabolism: a cross talk between gut microbiota and its human host.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>300-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1152/physiol.00023.2012</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The recent epidemic of obesity and diabetes and the diversity at the individual level could be explained by the intestinal microbiota-to-host relationship. More than four million gene products from the microbiome could interact with the immune system to induce a tissue metabolic infection, which is the molecular origin of the low-grade inflammation that characterizes the onset of obesity and diabetes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
